\subsection{Additional Analysis}
\label{sec:why_tlm_fail}

\paragraph{Error analysis.}
\label{sec:error_analysis}
Cross-agent, the probe errs on 19.9\% of OH windows vs.\ 0.51\% for GB---a 40$\times$ gap with near-disjoint errors (7.2\% in-domain; Appendix~\ref{sec:app_error_analysis}).

\paragraph{Outcome backpropagation.}
\label{sec:ob_analysis}
$\lambda_3$ contributes 33.5\% of conf${\geq}$2 labels while agreeing 100\% with 2-LF labels where both are defined; removing it costs 7.7\,pp (Appendix~\ref{sec:app_ob_analysis}).

\paragraph{GB vs.\ RF deployment trade-off.}
GB leads RF by 5.5\,pp on all-windows cross-agent transfer (0.967 vs.\ 0.912), but RF is more robust on conf${\geq}$2 (0.996 vs.\ 0.992) and under 2-LF label degradation ($-$1.8 vs.\ $-$12\,pp).
GB suits broad deployment; RF suits high-confidence settings; either enables 15--30\% compute savings via early termination (Appendix Figure~\ref{fig:pareto}).

